      "title": "Breakthrough curve",
      "description": "The bed works from the inlet down: the top becomes saturated (red), the mass-transfer zone (orange) moves down, and the outlet stays clean until the zone reaches the bottom — breakthrough. Activated alumina is used for drying gases and liquids (to dew points around −40 °C), fluoride and arsenic removal from water, and HCl/acid removal; it is regenerated by heating (drying duty) or chemically (e.g. caustic and acid for fluoride).",
